Part A — Triggers 14–20
76. AFTER DELETE trigger

The assignment asks for an AFTER DELETE trigger that stores deleted order details in a deleted_orders table.

Step 1 — Create the table
CREATE TABLE deleted_orders (
    order_id INT,
    customer_name VARCHAR(50),
    product_name VARCHAR(50),
    category VARCHAR(30),
    quantity INT,
    price DECIMAL(10,2),
    discount DECIMAL(5,2),
    city VARCHAR(30),
    order_date DATE,
    status VARCHAR(20)
);
Step 2 — Create the trigger
DELIMITER //

CREATE TRIGGER after_order_delete
AFTER DELETE ON sales_orders
FOR EACH ROW
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO deleted_orders
    VALUES (
        OLD.order_id,
        OLD.customer_name,
        OLD.product_name,
        OLD.category,
        OLD.quantity,
        OLD.price,
        OLD.discount,
        OLD.city,
        OLD.order_date,
        OLD.status
    );
END //

DELIMITER ;
Important

For DELETE, there is no NEW row.

We use:

OLD.column

because we're accessing the row that was deleted.

